   "relation": "family"
  },
  {
   "id": "mdx-jsx",
   "relation": "family"
  },
  {
   "id": "html",
   "relation": "compiles-to"
  }
 ],
 "level_notes": {
  "0": "Markdown.pl (Perl, 1.0.1 of 2004; 1.0.2b8 beta) is the reference implementation and in practice the definition. Ports that track its behaviour (PHP Markdown, Python-Markdown, Showdown, Discount, Redcarpet, kramdown, Parsedown) and later parsers (marked, markdown-it, md4c) are listed; the mdtest suite descends from Gruber's MarkdownTest.",
  "1": "There is no formal specification: Gruber's syntax page is descriptive and leaves many cases undefined. RFC 7763/7764 register the text/markdown media type and variant names; PHP Markdown Extra and MultiMarkdown documents define the most influential early extensions. CommonMark, GFM and Pandoc Markdown have their own entries.",
  "2": "The Markdown Guide is the main tutorial; Atwood's and MacFarlane's essays explain why the dialect fragmented.",
  "3": "Babelmark compares implementations side by side."
 },
